How can I enhance the machine learning model to analyze the tone and emotion of customer reviews more comprehensively using MATLAB? Here are the customer reviews in [Latext] format:
\begin{itemize}
\item Review 1: ``The product exceeded my expectations and the customer service was top-notch.''
\item Review 2: ``The product was subpar and the delivery was delayed multiple times.''
\end{itemize}
I have used the following MATLAB code to analyze the tone and emotion so far:
\begin{lstlisting}[language=Matlab]
reviews = {'The product exceeded my expectations and the customer service was top-notch.', 'The product was subpar and the delivery was delayed multiple times.'};
documents = tokenizedDocument(reviews);
bag = bagOfWords(documents);
positiveWords = {'exceeded', 'top-notch'};
negativeWords = {'subpar', 'delayed'};
positiveCounts = countWords(bag,positiveWords);
negativeCounts = countWords(bag,negativeWords);
positiveIndex = find(positiveCounts);
negativeIndex = find(negativeCounts);
sentiment = positiveIndex - negativeIndex;
\end{lstlisting}
However, I am looking for a more accurate and comprehensive approach to analyze customer reviews. Any suggestions or improvements to the current code using advanced techniques in machine learning or natural language processing?

