What is the MATLAB code to find 10 synonyms and antonyms each for the given word 'amazing' using the WordNet database? Additionally, can you provide a table comparing the sentiment and connotation of the word 'amazing' and its synonyms and antonyms? Please use the following categories: positive, neutral, negative, formal, informal, slang. Here is the code to start with:
word = 'amazing';
synonyms = [];
antonyms = [];
wnObj = javaObject('edu.smu.tspell.wordnet.WordNetDatabase');
wnpath = wnObj.getPath();
idx = strfind(wnpath, filesep());
idx = idx(end);
wnpath = wnpath(1:idx-1);
wnObj = javaObject('edu.smu.tspell.wordnet.WordNetDatabase');
wnObj.setDirectory(wnpath);
synsets = wnObj.getSynsets(word);
for i=1:min(10,length(synsets))
    synonyms = [synonyms, synsets(i).getWordForms()];
end
for i=1:min(10,length(synsets))
    antonyms = [antonyms, synsets(i).getAntonyms()];
end
disp(synonyms);
disp(antonyms);
